Hello,

While writing the wikia article on compiling and patching
NetHack under Windows, I decided to take a look at how hard
it would be to make menucolors work under the Window GUI version.

Not too hard, apparently, even though this was about my first
time compiling anything under windows.

The following zip-file contains both the GUI and TTY versions,
with menucolors patched in.  No regular expressions, only
globbing (that is, ? and * wildcards, like in DOS filenames),
and the GUI menucolors don't obey the attributes you define.

http://bilious.homelinux.org/~paxed/nethack/nh343-menucolors.zip


I'll update the menucolors patch when I've cleaned up the new GUI
parts a bit.

